{
  "summary": "The mult_ctrl controller exhibits a fixed 8-cycle latency from start to done for every value of secret_operand, which satisfies a naive constant-time expectation. However, this constant latency does NOT prevent side-channel leakage: the mul_en signal is asserted on cycle k (1<=k<=8) if and only if bit (8-k) of secret_operand is set, so the total number of cycles with mul_en=1 during the fixed 8-cycle transaction window (enable_count) equals the Hamming weight (popcount) of secret_operand. An observer monitoring switching activity (e.g. power or EM activity correlated with mul_en-gated accumulator updates) during the known-length transaction window can simply count active cycles and directly recover the Hamming weight of secret_operand from a single trace, independent of the fact that done always fires exactly 8 cycles after start. Constant done/product timing therefore provides no protection against this activity-based leakage channel.",
  "timing_analysis": {
    "observed_latency_cycles": 8,
    "latency_is_constant": true
  },
